1
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Black Cadillacs is a drama film directed by Marlida Ferreira.

2
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
The story of two friends on leave after serving in Afghanistan.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Together they make the trip home for thanksgiving
where friends and family await.

4
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
They reminisce and question if one can ever really go back home.

5
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Rua, played by Shannon Barnett.

6
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Tighe, played by Sean Clement.

7
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Siobhan, played by Rachel Gassi.

8
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Finn, played by PJ Lazic.

9
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Catherine, played by Tamsen McDonough.

10
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Alana, played by Patricia McKenzie.

11
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
"Two Black Cadillacs" is a song by American recording artist Carrie
Underwood, taken from her fourth studio album, Blown Away.

12
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
The song served as the album's third single on
November 18, 2012, through Arista Nashville.

13
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Written by Underwood, Hillary Lindsey, and Josh Kear, "Two Black Cadillacs" features lyrics addressing the story
of two women who, when they realize they are both involved with the same man, decide to kill him.

14
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
It was produced by Mark Bright, and the instrumentation was
compared to songs by Dixie Chicks and Miranda Lambert.

15
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Upon its release, "Two Black Cadillacs" was met with positive reviews from music
critics, who praised its story and Underwood's versatility as an artist.

16
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Commercially, the song was successful.

17
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:46,000
In the United States, it reached number two on the Billboard Country
Airplay chart, and also reached number 41 on the Hot 100.

18
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
As of July 2020, "Two Black Cadillacs" was certified 2× Platinum by
the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA).

19
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
The song also charted in Canada at number three on the Country
chart and at number 52 on the Canadian Hot 100.

20
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:46,000
The accompanying music video was directed by P.R.

21
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Brown, and filmed in Nashville, Tennessee.

22
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:26,000
The video draws inspiration from Stephen King's novel Christine, and shows how the
wife and mistress kill the cheating husband with a black Cadillac.

23
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:46,000
It was nominated for Video of the Year at the 2013
Academy of Country Music Awards.

24
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Underwood has performed "Two Black Cadillacs" in a number of live appearances, including at the 55th Annual Grammy Awards, where various images were
projected onto the singer's gown, and at the 2013 Country Music Association Awards, in a medley with "Good Girl", "See You Again", and "Blown Away".

25
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:26,000
It was also performed during the Blown Away Tour.

26
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
The tone is emotional.
